  "description": "This thoroughbred racing horse has proved itself on the World Cup circuit and has been chosen by countless privateers for its renown reliability and performance. This version of the Fuzz is not just the old bike with revised geometry to suit big wheels. The frame has been completely re-designed and features a badass forged one-piece rocker that adds rigidity to the rear end and drives a modern trunnion shock. It has a low center of gravity, with the shock tucked away near the BB, adjustable reach via offset cups and an option of choosing internal or external cable routing. The suspension kinematics have been tailored to provide exceptional ride characteristics. There is a significant amount of rearward axle movement that helps smooth out square faced bumps, and there is plenty of anti-squat built in which minimizes suspension bob when pedaling. The reach has a 16mm range of adjustability via the eccentric headset.\nINTENDED USE CATEGORY 7: DOWNHILL, FREERIDE & ENDURO\nTough alloy frame with double pass welds\nRadical geo with adjustable reach\none-piece forged rocker WITH trunion shock\n200mm front / 190mm rear travel\nFOX suspension WITH AIR FORK & SHOCK\nsram gx 7spd drivetrain\nHayes Dominion A4 4 piston brakes\nOFFSET HEADSET CUPS ALLOW REACH TO BE ADJUSTED\nReach can be adjusted by +/- 8mm.\nMASSIVE ONE PIECE ROCKER\nKeeps the longer rear end of the 29” bike incredibly stiff.\n4-BAR HORST LINK SUSPENSION\n4-BAR HORST LINK SUSPENSION with unique floating shock design\nMODERN GEOMETRY\nOne of the most progressive on the market",
